[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260184344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3260184344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3260184344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CUncY","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T01:37:37Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T01:37:37Z","body":"To anyone reviewing this: although the `srgb_to_linear` function shown in this issue doesn't have the typical constants (`12.92`, `1.055`, etc.), it appears to be correct with minor rounding error: it's just a different mathematical representation of the same function that avoids using division and replaces it with multiplication.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260184344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260341800","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3260341800","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3260341800,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CVN4o","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T03:48:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T03:48:45Z","body":"Viewport textures give you access to the output of the 2D rendertarget which is an SDR texture after `linear_to_srgb()` conversion has been applied. So it is completely expected that converting it back into linear space will make it appear the same as the texture when it is already in linear space. \n\nFor context, the typical rendering path godot takes (when HDR2D is not enabled is:\n1. Render 3D content to an HDR buffer in with linear encoding\n2. Convert the HDR values into LDR, then compress with srgb gamma encoding\n3. Render 2D content\n4. Copy texture to the screen\n\nWhen you read from the \"render buffer\" in a compositor effect, you are retrieving the HDR buffer in step 1. It has a high precision and uses a linear encoding. \n\nWhen you read from a ViewportTexture you are reading the buffer after step 3. So you are reading an LDR texture with srgb gamma encoding. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260341800/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260517690","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3260517690","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3260517690,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CV406","user":{"login":"th317erd","id":4420452,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjA0NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4420452?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd","html_url":"https://github.com/th317erd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T04:21:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T04:21:22Z","body":"I've got a very similar situation which is really messing things up for me. I have tried every possible solution I can find online, but no matter what I do, the colors are changing on the texture rendered by the SubViewport.\n\nI have TWO SubViewports in use, because the first one down samples the full-sized scene render for more efficient shader computation, and the second takes the output from the first shader computation, and does further shader computation, before the result is finally rendered to the PrimaryCamera (quad in front of it actually).\n\nSee the screenshot I have attached. I can set the color DIRECTLY on \"ALBEDO\" in the first shader, and then read it directly (with an \"if\" statement to debug the value) in the second shader, and the value has indeed changed.\n\nHow can I prevent Godot changing the uniform texture on me? Why is it changing the colors? Please help! I am losing hair!\n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1413\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/03a66dc8-e792-4d3c-9752-97489a5f1785\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260517690/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260926644","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3260926644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3260926644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CXcq0","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T05:22:59Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T05:24:36Z","body":"@th317erd you can enable HDR2D in the project settings. Otherwise Godot will render the 2D viewport in sRGB (which is what you are reading when you read from a Viewport Texture)\n\nIf you are reading the Viewport Texture in a GDShader, you can also use hint_color to tell the GDShader that you have an input in sRGB space, but when you sample from it you want the result to be linear","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260926644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260970323","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3260970323","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3260970323,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CXnVT","user":{"login":"th317erd","id":4420452,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjA0NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4420452?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd","html_url":"https://github.com/th317erd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T05:30:43Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T05:30:43Z","body":"@clayjohn I have tried that. I have tried pretty much everything I have found online. Both my spatial shaders attached to Quad meshes in-front of camera's for the SubViewports have the following at the top of the shader:\n\n```\nshader_type spatial;\n\nuniform sampler2D screen_tex : hint_screen_texture, repeat_disable;\nuniform sampler2D view_port_tex : source_color;\n\nrender_mode unshaded, fog_disabled, depth_draw_opaque, blend_mix;\n```\n\nI have debugged a LOT with \"if\" statements, and the color values are fluctuating in ways I can't understand. Can you think of anything else that might be causing this trouble?\n\nI have no world or environment, and yet a horizon is being rendered. I have been wondering if it is the environment changing things (even though I have requested \"unshaded\" in the shader).\n\nThoughts?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260970323/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3261044930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3261044930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3261044930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CX5jC","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T05:43:33Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T05:43:33Z","body":"@th317erd with that amount of information I can't say much. You are certainly in a very different situation from the OP of this big report though. \n\nIf you suspect that you are running into a bug, feel free to open a bug report and fill out the template as well as provide a full MRP. Then  I (or another contributor) can take a look. \n\nJust from looking at those two lines though, I can see that one texture will be linear and the other one will be sRGB. So if you are relying on pixel comparisons you will definitely get different values (the screen texture is HDR while the Viewport texture is LDR). They are also both using mipmaps. So those could be coming into play as well. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3261044930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3261079941","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3261079941","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3261079941,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CYCGF","user":{"login":"th317erd","id":4420452,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjA0NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4420452?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd","html_url":"https://github.com/th317erd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T05:49:06Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T05:52:07Z","body":"@clayjohn Would you be willing to look at my repository if I was to invite you? I'd be very grateful.\n\nEdit: Maybe I/we would be able to help the OP when I finally understand what I am doing wrong.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3261079941/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3262388461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3262388461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3262388461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CdBjt","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T15:14:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T15:34:50Z","body":"I would try to force the `[Viewport.use_hdr_2d](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_viewport.html#class-viewport-property-use-hdr-2d)` property to `true` on all viewports at runtime, such as in the `_ready()` method of the viewports. Do this in addition to setting the project setting `rendering/viewport/hdr_2d` to `true`. Finally make sure you're using the Mobile or Forward+ renderer.\n\nMy suspicion is that you have HDR 2D set to `false` on one of your viewports, but if that's not the case, then you'll need to open an issue with a minimum reproduction project. Sharing the whole project isn't within the scope of what we can do here on the Godot development GitHub.\n\nAnother possibility is that you actually want nonlinear sRGB encoded values, but you're getting linear encoded values instead. If you need more help than this, you can ask around [elsewhere](https://godotengine.org/community/), as this place is intended for engine development rather than game development.\n\nEdit: ah, I see clayjohn has helped out already a fair bit and I see that in your screenshot the selected viewport has `use_hdr_2d` disabled in the property inspector.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3262388461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263173853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3263173853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3263173853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CgBTd","user":{"login":"th317erd","id":4420452,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjA0NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4420452?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd","html_url":"https://github.com/th317erd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T20:02:41Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T20:04:37Z","body":"@allenwp Thank you for your guidance. I have tried everything I can find online, including what you recommend. I even tried manually fudging the colors with `linear_to_srgb` (and inverse) functions just to try and make sense of this.\n\nI know that I want linear color space, NOT sRGB, because I am encoding values in bits between shaders. I don't want any modification of the bits I am encoding.\n\nI am trying to contribute here. I am not trying to hijack this bug report, nor am I asking for help with \"Game Development\". There is obviously something wrong, as this is undocumented, and I can not find any assistance online... just like the OP.\n\nI am happy to continue to try and help with the OPs problem, which appears the same as mine. Here I have made publicly available a minimal example that shows the issue. I figured I would just post it here instead of creating an unnecessary new bug report, because I feel me and the OP likely do have the same issue.\n\nPlease take a look when you have a moment. I have created a README as a guide, and also have many comments in the code to explain what is going on, and what is going wrong.\n\nI am using Godot 4.4 with the Forward+ renderer.\n\nhttps://github.com/th317erd/godot-color-issues\n\nEdit: Oh, and I am happy to assist with a bug fix when someone helps me identify the problem (if it is indeed a bug). I am happy to fix it and create a PR. I am not shy about contributing. I just need some guidance here.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263173853/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263235446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3263235446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3263235446,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CgQV2","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T21:37:24Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T21:37:24Z","body":"@th317erd Please open a bug report if you think you are running into a bug. There is a reason we have a template and a defined process. You are feeding Allen and I bits of information which is the least efficient way to solve a problem. Further, its not even clear that there is a bug with Godot. It is extremely rude to demand contributors take a look at your project and give you personal assistance.\n\nAt this point you have fully derailed this bug report since the issue you have is not the same as the one that the OP has. \n\nWe have already fully resolved the OPs issue. Now all that remains is to decide whether this is something that calls for better documentation or if we can go ahead and close the issue. Please read my first comment on this bug report for an explanation about what OP is misunderstanding. \n\nI ask again, please open a bug report and follow the proper bug reporting procedure if you think what you are encountering is a bug. If you are unsure whether your issue is a bug, please use one of the various community channels for assistance instead of clogging up our bug reporting channels. We are very short on contributors and we simply don't have the time to personally dive into every user's project whenever they get stuck. Please respect that. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263235446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263262417","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3263262417","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3263262417,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CgW7R","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T22:36:59Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T22:36:59Z","body":"Actually, I took a look at your project. The problem is indeed with your shader. You are treating the 16 bit SNORM texture as if it is a 16 bit UINT texture. Because of that, you are running into floating point precision errors. Your method of packing 15 bits into a single half float loses a lot of precision in the process. Particularly, since red is in the lowest bits, it is subject to precision loss when you convert to a half float and ends up basically either returning 0.5 or 1.0\n\nIf you pack your color values properly, then the issue will go away. \n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263262417/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3272547926","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110277#issuecomment-3272547926","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110277","id":3272547926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DDx5W","user":{"login":"th317erd","id":4420452,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjA0NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4420452?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd","html_url":"https://github.com/th317erd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th317erd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-09T23:01:35Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T23:01:35Z","body":"@clayjohn Thank you. I greatly appreciate your assistance.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/com